            <ArticleTitle>Lamotrigine control of central pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>179-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Central pain remains a therapeutic challenge. We report beneficial effects of lamotrigine, a novel antiepileptic drug, on four patients suffering from long-standing central pain. Analgesia may be due to interference with glutamatergic transmission.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
